            <div itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Person" class="image-text">
                <span itemprop="name">Addy Osmani</span> is an <span itemprop="nationality">Irish</span> <a itemprop="jobTitle" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/addyosmani/">engineering and evangelism leader</a> and a Member of Technical Staff at <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/">Anthropic</a>. He works on Claude Code. He spent over 14 years at Google, most recently as a Director at <a href="https://cloud.google.com/ai">Google Cloud AI</a>, running Cloud AI Developer Experience and Technical Evangelism and helping launch Google's agent developer platform. Before that he led Developer Experience across <a href="https://www.google.com/chrome/">Chrome</a>, DevTools, Lighthouse, and Core Web Vitals, and <a href="https://gemini.addy.ie">Gemini's</a> developer experience (coding agents, evals, code quality). A developer for 25+ years, and earlier an engineer on <a href="https://golden.com/wiki/Addy_Osmani_(software_engineer)-REKEB86">Fortune 500 sites</a>, he is passionate about AI-assisted engineering and developer tools. He is the <a itemprop="author" href="https://g.co/kgs/t9AVE7">author</a> of <a href="https://store.addy.ie">books</a> including <a itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Book" href="https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/learning-javascript-design/9781449334840/"><span itemprop="title">Learning JavaScript Design Patterns</span></a>, <a href="https://leet.addy.ie">Leading Effective Engineering Teams</a>, <a href="https://stoic.addy.ie">Stoic Mind</a>, and <a itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Book" href="https://www.smashingmagazine.com/printed-books/image-optimization/"><span itemprop="title">Image Optimization</span></a>, and has given over 200 <a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLVUliVBcvz1lKS9-rcPFFXkwGOj_YX_-5">talks</a> worldwide. You can find his writing on his <a href="https://addyosmani.com/blog/">blog</a>, <a href="https://substack.com/@addyosmani">Substack</a>, and <a href="https://leaddev.com/community/addy-osmani">LeadDev</a>, his code in <a href="https://addyosmani.com/open-source">open source</a>, and him on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/addyosmani">LinkedIn</a>, <a href="https://twitter.com/addyosmani">Twitter</a>, and <a href="https://tiktok.com/@vvoicemotivation">TikTok</a>. 
